From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shayne <8741557+shaynelegault@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:06:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: apple-sftl: Reclaim closed data blocks in the write path

Track checkpoint and replay ownership across the whole device. Recover the map independently and verify native footer records before recycling an obsolete block. Reserve a blank landing block for mixed victims only when a checkpoint backend can install and retire a generation. Verify relocation, checkpoint readback and fresh recovery before erasing the donor, then make its capacity available to normal writes.

Exercise write pressure, cold recovery, interrupted summaries, ambiguous erase, retryable reservation failure and sequence exhaustion on synthetic media. Keep the P105 append-only until native checkpoint rotation and physical erase are qualified.

Assisted-by: LLM
